{"id":"a11","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":9,"of":19,"title":"This one and that one","titleHe":"זֶה וְזֹאת","goal":"Point at something — and know why this book has the article twice.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"זֶה is this for a masculine noun, זֹאת for a feminine one, and אֵלֶּה for either in the plural. They do two different jobs, and Hebrew writes them differently depending on which."},{"type":"text","body":"Standing alone in front of a noun, it means this is: זֶה סֵפֶר, this is a book. Standing after a definite noun, it means this: הַסֵּפֶר הַזֶּה, this book — and the article is repeated, exactly as an adjective repeats it."},{"type":"table","caption":"The four forms","head":["","alone — this is","after the noun — this"],"rows":[["m. sing.","זֶה — this is","הַזֶּה"],["f. sing.","זֹאת — this is","הַזֹּאת"],["m. plural","אֵלֶּה — these are","הָאֵלֶּה"],["f. plural","אֵלֶּה — these are","הָאֵלֶּה"]]},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"זֶה סֵפֶר טוֹב.","en":"This is a good book."},{"he":"הַסֵּפֶר הַזֶּה טוֹב.","en":"This book is good."},{"he":"זֹאת הַמּוֹרָה שֶׁלִּי.","en":"This is my teacher."},{"he":"הַיְלָדִים הָאֵלֶּה גְּדוֹלִים.","en":"These children are big."},{"he":"מָה זֶה?","en":"What is this?"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"For that rather than this, Hebrew reuses the third-person pronoun: הָאִישׁ הַהוּא, that man; הָאִשָּׁה הַהִיא, that woman. In speech people mostly say הַזֶּה and point."},{"type":"tip","body":"Speech is looser than the table. Plenty of Israelis say זֶה where the book wants זֹאת, and אֵלּוּ turns up for אֵלֶּה in writing. Read both, write the table."}],"vocab":[{"he":"זֹאת","en":"this (f.)","translit":"zot"},{"he":"אֵלֶּה","en":"these","translit":"ele"},{"he":"הַזֶּה","en":"this (after the noun, m.)","translit":"haze"},{"he":"הַזֹּאת","en":"this (after the noun, f.)","translit":"hazot"},{"he":"הָהוּא","en":"that (m.)","translit":"hahu"},{"he":"כָּזֶה","en":"like this, such a","translit":"kaze"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["receives","cousin (m.)","Nisan (Mar–Apr)","this (f.)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"זֹאת","translit":"zot"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["these","wanderings","than her","cheese"],"correct":0,"prompt":"אֵלֶּה","translit":"ele"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["behold, here is","mother","flame, blade","this (after the noun, m.)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"הַזֶּה","translit":"haze"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["this (after the noun, f.)","gate","ring","a quorum of ten"],"correct":0,"prompt":"הַזֹּאת","translit":"hazot"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["Gemara","the city","known","that (m.)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"הָהוּא","translit":"hahu"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["like this, such a","at most","went","happy holiday"],"correct":0,"prompt":"כָּזֶה","translit":"kaze"},{"type":"read","he":"הַזֹּאת","translit":"hazot","en":"this (after the noun, f.)"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “like this, such a”?","options":["לִלְמֹד","כָּזֶה","כַּמּוּת","כָּאן"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"m. sing.?","options":["הַזֹּאת","הָאֵלֶּה","הַזֶּה","הָאֵלֶּה"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"___ הַזֶּה טוֹב.","en":"This book is good.","options":["זֹאת","הַסֵּפֶר","הַזֶּה","כָּזֶה"],"correct":1,"full":"הַסֵּפֶר הַזֶּה טוֹב."},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “this (f.)”?","options":["לְעֻמַּת","זֹאת","מַחֲשָׁבָה","נִרְאֶה"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["זֹאת","this (f.)"],["אֵלֶּה","these"],["הַזֶּה","this (after the noun, m.)"],["הַזֹּאת","this (after the noun, f.)"],["הָהוּא","that (m.)"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"f. sing.?","options":["הַזֶּה","הַזֹּאת","הָאֵלֶּה","הָאֵלֶּה"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"build","tokens":["טוֹב","הַזֶּה","הַסֵּפֶר"],"answer":["הַסֵּפֶר","הַזֶּה","טוֹב"],"en":"This book is good."},{"type":"build","tokens":["שֶׁלִּי","זֹאת","הַמּוֹרָה"],"answer":["זֹאת","הַמּוֹרָה","שֶׁלִּי"],"en":"This is my teacher."},{"type":"type","q":"Write “this (after the noun, m.)” in Hebrew","answer":"הַזֶּה","hint":"haze"}]}